# Frontend Rules

## Structure

```
frontend/src/
  components/     # Reusable UI (TodoItem, TodoForm)
  hooks/          # useTodos.js — data fetching and state
  api/            # fetch wrappers (todos.js)
  App.jsx
  main.jsx
```

- One component per file; filename matches component name (`TodoList.jsx`).
- Colocate component-specific CSS only when tiny; prefer shared styles in `index.css`.

## Components

```jsx
// ✅ GOOD — small, focused, typed props via JSDoc if not using TypeScript
/**
 * @param {{ todo: { id: number, title: string, completed: boolean }, onToggle: (id: number) => void }} props
 */
export function TodoItem({ todo, onToggle }) {
  return (
    <li>
      <input
        type="checkbox"
        checked={todo.completed}
        onChange={() => onToggle(todo.id)}
        aria-label={`Mark "${todo.title}" as ${todo.completed ? 'incomplete' : 'complete'}`}
      />
      <span className={todo.completed ? 'completed' : undefined}>{todo.title}</span>
    </li>
  )
}
```

- Use function components and hooks only — no class components.
- Extract `useTodos()` hook when more than one component needs todo state.

## Data fetching

- Centralize API calls in `src/api/` — components should not hardcode URLs.

```javascript
// ✅ GOOD — api/todos.js
const BASE = import.meta.env.VITE_API_URL ?? 'http://localhost:5000/api'

export async function fetchTodos() {
  const res = await fetch(`${BASE}/todos`)
  if (!res.ok) throw new Error('Failed to load todos')
  return res.json()
}
```

- Handle loading, empty, and error states in the UI — never assume fetch succeeds.
- Use `async/await` with try/catch; show a user-friendly message on failure.

## State

```jsx
// ❌ BAD — mutating state directly
todos.push(newTodo)
setTodos(todos)

// ✅ GOOD — immutable update
setTodos((prev) => [...prev, newTodo])
```

- Prefer lifting state only as high as needed; avoid prop drilling past 2 levels — use context or a hook.

## Styling

- Aim for clean, practical UI: clear spacing, readable font size (16px base), visible focus states.
- Use CSS variables in `:root` for colors so theming stays consistent.
- Mobile-first or at least responsive down to 320px width.

## Accessibility

- Every form input needs a `<label>` or `aria-label`.
- Use semantic HTML: `<main>`, `<ul>`, `<button type="button">` (not `<div onClick>`).
- Keyboard: todos must be toggled and submitted without a mouse.

## Tooling

- Run `npm run lint` before committing; fix oxlint errors.
- Use `VITE_API_URL` env var for the backend base URL — never hardcode production URLs.

## Bad habits to avoid

- Fetching inside every component render — fetch in `useEffect` or event handlers.
- Missing dependency arrays or stale closures in hooks.
- Inline styles for everything — use classes for repeated patterns.
- Ignoring loading spinners and empty states ("No todos yet").
- Duplicating validation that already exists on the backend (frontend validation is UX only).
